/*
This script creates a JTree that can be used for browsing a user interface.  
As each node is selected, it can be referenced by 'y.selected'.
Note:  It is usually safest and most common to browse JPanel's
vs JFrame's/JInternalFrame's.  Also, you don't have to place your
target JPanel into the swingbrowser center panel... it is just available
if you wish to use it such as building a prototype UI.
The swingbrowser can browse any JPanel you give it via the treemodel.
*/

